## Ⅳ. PASSAGE FLOW

```
BOL (know the boundary) → GAT (find the gate) → RIT (cross with ceremony)

BOL: "This is the boundary between sandbox and production"
GAT: "Gate C controls this boundary; it is AMBER; threshold = 0.85 consensus"
RIT: "Crossing requires the deployment ceremony: VERIFICATOR audit + FABRICATOR sign"

No one crosses a boundary without knowing it exists (BOL).
No one passes a gate without permission or proof (GAT).
No one transitions without the ceremony being witnessed (RIT).
```

